Understood, so I'll keep the existing function signature and add a compatibility path. Here's the core of it:

ts
export function toUtcIntervals(slots: Slot[], date: string, zone: string): Interval[] {
  return slots.map(s => ({
    start: zonedTimeToUtc(`${date} ${s.start}`, zone).getTime(),
    end: zonedTimeToUtc(`${date} ${s.end}`, zone).getTime(),
  }));
}


Then `findOverlap` intersects those epoch intervals across all members. I'll also add tests for a DST transition weekend, since that's where naive math usually breaks again.
